1
00:00:53,603 --> 00:00:56,581
How about some music?

2
00:00:56,581 --> 00:00:59,559
No, let's wait till Robbie gets back from the airport.

3
00:00:59,559 --> 00:01:02,537
Did she say why she had to leave today?

4
00:01:02,537 --> 00:01:04,409
She told Robbie that her flight tomorrow was canceled,

5
00:01:04,409 --> 00:01:07,515
so she had to take an earlier flight today.

6
00:01:07,515 --> 00:01:08,493
This is terrible.

7
00:01:08,493 --> 00:01:11,471
Well, that must be him.

8
00:01:11,471 --> 00:01:12,911
Why is he blowing his horn like that?

9
00:01:12,911 --> 00:01:13,631
I don't know.

10
00:01:13,631 --> 00:01:14,449
Maybe he's angry.

11
00:01:14,449 --> 00:01:16,449
Do you think we should take down the decorations?

12
00:01:16,449 --> 00:01:17,427
They'll just make him sad.

13
00:01:17,427 --> 00:01:18,174
Too late now.

14
00:01:18,174 --> 00:01:20,405
We should have done it sooner.

15
00:01:20,405 --> 00:01:23,383
Oh, here he comes.

16
00:01:23,383 --> 00:01:24,183
Hi.

17
00:01:24,183 --> 00:01:25,383
How'd it go?

18
00:01:25,383 --> 00:01:27,218
OK, I guess.

19
00:01:27,218 --> 00:01:30,251
Especially when Alexandra gave me a surprise ...

20
00:01:30,251 --> 00:01:31,349
Yeah? What was it?

21
00:01:31,349 --> 00:01:31,594
This!

22
00:01:31,594 --> 00:01:38,273
Alexandra! Alexandra

23
00:01:38,273 --> 00:01:41,251
Hi! What happened?

24
00:01:41,251 --> 00:01:44,229
I called my parents from the airport.

25
00:01:44,229 --> 00:01:45,229
When I told them

26
00:01:45,229 --> 00:01:46,979
my friends were giving me a party,

27
00:01:46,979 --> 00:01:49,336
they insisted that I stay.

28
00:01:49,336 --> 00:01:53,163
So now I'm taking a flight on Monday instead.

29
00:01:53,163 --> 00:01:53,763
That's great! Terrific!

30
00:01:53,763 --> 00:01:56,426
But how did you know the party was for you?

31
00:01:56,426 --> 00:01:58,890
Well, Robbie told me when he gave me this.

32
00:01:58,890 --> 00:02:02,096
Oh, it's so pretty!

33
00:02:02,096 --> 00:02:02,846
It's lovely, Robbie.

34
00:02:02,846 --> 00:02:03,346
All right!

35
00:02:03,346 --> 00:02:06,274
Now we can really start the party!

36
00:02:06,274 --> 00:02:07,474
No. Would you mind?

37
00:02:07,474 --> 00:02:10,852
I'd like to say something first.

38
00:02:10,852 --> 00:02:11,370
Hear, hear!

39
00:02:11,370 --> 00:02:14,738
I would just like to thank all of you,

40
00:02:14,738 --> 00:02:15,468
my friends,

41
00:02:15,468 --> 00:02:21,164
who have made my stay in the United States so wonderful.

42
00:02:21,164 --> 00:02:23,442
And to Robbie and the Stewart family

43
00:02:23,442 --> 00:02:25,692
for opening their home to me.

44
00:02:25,692 --> 00:02:26,738
We should thank you.

45
00:02:26,738 --> 00:02:27,829
You're a real friend!

46
00:02:27,829 --> 00:02:32,209
And I also have a little surprise for you, Robbie.

47
00:02:32,209 --> 00:02:33,876
A little going-away present.

48
00:02:33,876 --> 00:02:34,854
Thank you.

49
00:02:34,854 --> 00:02:36,105
Open it, please.

50
00:02:36,105 --> 00:02:38,792
I think you might be amused.

51
00:02:38,792 --> 00:02:43,788
OK. I can't believe it!

52
00:02:43,788 --> 00:02:46,766
I guess we were thinking the same thought.

53
00:02:46,766 --> 00:03:17,545
You had it engraved!

54
00:03:17,545 --> 00:03:54,852
Read it, Robbie.

55
00:03:54,852 --> 00:04:04,193
"In friendship, always. Alexandra." “

56
00:04:04,193 --> 00:04:09,779
I knew we thought alike,

57
00:04:09,779 --> 00:04:22,489
but this is too much!

58
00:04:22,489 --> 00:04:29,216
Thank you.

59
00:04:29,216 --> 00:04:53,840
All right!

60
00:04:53,840 --> 00:04:58,796
Let's have some music!

61
00:04:58,796 --> 00:05:03,274
Miss Pappas? Pappas

62
00:05:03,274 --> 00:05:07,717
Mr. Stewart ... Stewart

63
00:05:07,717 --> 00:05:15,664
Mrs. Stewart, may I have this dance? Stewart

64
00:05:15,664 --> 00:05:18,664
My pleasure, Doctor.
